  "id": "COMPOUND:22598 - PROTEIN:4953",
  "verbalization": "Crassocolide F is implicated in the activation of EDD domain protein, DegV family, which in turn targets HEp-2 cells. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which point to a shared mechanism of action involving the EDD domain protein. The evidence suggests that Crassocolide F acts as a ligand that binds to the EDD domain of DegV family proteins, initiating a cascade of events that ultimately lead to the interaction with HEp-2 cells. The consistent presence of HEp-2 as a target across different pathways underscores the significance of this cellular response. The integration of these findings highlights a potential role for Crassocolide F in modulating cellular processes through the EDD domain protein, suggesting a broader biological impact on HEp-2 cell function.",
